  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThe \"Cool Atmosphere\" look wraps the image in a gentle teal-green hue, casting a moody, cinematic vibe. The cool tones soften the scene, adding a serene, introspective quality. Blues shift subtly toward teal, while greens deepen, enriching the environment. Skin tones are cooled down, giving a slightly desaturated, ethereal appearance. Shadows are present but not harsh, maintaining a balanced contrast. This look brings a sense of calm and reflection. It’s ideal for indoor scenes where you want to capture a soft, cool atmosphere.\n\nWhen using this recipe, we recommend setting [Active D-Lighting] to [Extra high] or [Extra high 1] on your camera. Selecting either of these options preserves details in highlights while achieving rich, cinema-like tonal gradations in your image.",
